"{OK}\n"
"\n"
"Exit this menu."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.1"
msgid ""
"{Music}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle ambient music level."
msgstr ""
"{Music}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle ambient music level.\n"
"\n"
"(Note: When using CD Stereo music in DOS, the music may only be turned on or off - the level has no effect.)"

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.2"
msgid ""
"{Effects}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle foreground sounds level."
msgstr ""
"{Effects}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle foreground sounds level."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.3"
msgid ""
"{Speed}\n"
"\n"
"Change the speed at which your heroes move on the main screen."
msgstr ""
"{Speed}\n"
"\n"
"Change the speed at which your heroes move on the main screen."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.4"
msgid ""
"{Music Type}\n"
"\n"
"Heroes II uses MIDI music."
msgstr ""
"{Music Type}\n"
"\n"
"Change the type of music.  MIDI music does not usually sound as good, but hurts performance less than CD Stereo.  If you use CD Stereo, you can select whether or not to have the operatic town themes play or not.\n"
"\n"
"(Note: Some older computers do not handle CD Stereo music well.  If you have a computer that leaves the music playing when you quit or crashes when you switch music tracks, try MIDI music.)"

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.5"
msgid ""
"{Show Path}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle 'Show Path' on/off.  If 'Show Path' is on, your first click on a map location will show the path to get there, your second will start you moving. If this option is off, one click starts you moving immediately."
msgstr ""
"{Show Path}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle 'Show Path' on/off.  If 'Show Path' is on, your first click on a map location will show the path to get there, your second will start you moving. If this option is off, one click starts you moving immediately."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.6"
msgid ""
"{Enemy Speed}\n"
"\n"
"Sets the speed that A.I. heroes move at.  You can also elect not to view A.I. movement at all."
msgstr ""
"{Enemy Speed}\n"
"\n"
"Sets the speed that A.I. heroes move at.  You can also elect not to view A.I. movement at all."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.7"
msgid ""
"{Interface}\n"
"\n"
"Sets what type of interface you want to use.  The default selection is a dynamic interface, which uses Evil graphics for the 3 evil heroes (Barbarian, Warlock, and Necromancer)."
msgstr ""
"{Interface}\n"
"\n"
"Sets what type of interface you want to use.  The default selection is a dynamic interface, which uses Evil graphics for the 3 evil heroes (Barbarian, Warlock, and Necromancer)."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.8"
msgid ""
"{Video}\n"
"\n"
"Determines if the video sequences play normally or in interlaced mode. Interlaced mode runs better on slower machines."
msgstr ""
"{Video}\n"
"\n"
"Determines if the video sequences play normally or in interlaced mode.  Interlaced mode runs better on slower machines, or machines with double-speed CD drives."

#. Legacy table entry; English is authoritative in the C++ initializer.
#: src/SOURCE/KB.cpp
msgctxt "table.gSPanelHelp.9"
msgid ""
"{Mouse Cursor}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle color cursors on/off.  Color cursors look nicer, but sometimes don't move as smoothly as black and white ones."
msgstr ""
"{Mouse Cursor}\n"
"\n"
"Toggle color cursors on/off.  Color cursors look nicer, but sometimes don't move as smoothly as black and white ones."

